        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(opencode): Zen GPT-5.6 models are missing from discovery",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where OpenCode Zen users could not discover or resolve the `gpt-5.6-luna`, `gpt-5.6-terra`, and `gpt-5.6-sol` models even though OpenCode's live model catalog already advertised them.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe provider-owned Zen catalog now includes the three live GPT-5.6 routes with their OpenCode routing, context/output limits, pricing tiers, and supported reasoning efforts. The OpenCode thinking policy also exposes those declared `xhigh` and `max` levels while leaving proxied Claude profiles unchanged.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOpenCode Zen users can now see and select all three GPT-5.6 tiers through OpenClaw model discovery, including when the static catalog fallback is used, without `xhigh` or `max` being silently clamped to `high`.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Third-party live red: `https://opencode.ai/zen/v1/models` returned `gpt-5.6-luna`, `gpt-5.6-terra`, and `gpt-5.6-sol`; the OpenClaw live catalog contract failed with those exact three IDs reported as missing static metadata.\n- Credentialed third-party live suite: both OpenCode live tests passed, covering catalog alignment plus a real tool-call/reasoning replay through the provider.\n- Credentialed OpenClaw CLI E2E: `gpt-5.6-luna`, `gpt-5.6-terra`, and `gpt-5.6-sol` were each invoked with `--thinking max` through `https://opencode.ai/zen/v1/responses`; all calls returned HTTP 200 with reasoning-token usage and `aborted: false`.\n- OpenClaw CLI E2E on the final commit: the repository source completed its TypeScript and bundled-plugin build, then `models list --provider opencode --json` returned 55 models including all three GPT-5.6 routes with 1,050,000-token context windows. The command used isolated OpenClaw state directories.\n- Review reproduction red: both the bundled public policy artifact and registered provider surface silently omitted `xhigh`/`max` for the new GPT-5.6 routes; focused tests failed 2 cases.\n- Review fix green: the same focused policy tests passed 18/18, including `max` remaining available with the provider-owned profile.\n- OpenCode extension suite: 5 files, 35/35 tests passed.\n- Extension source and extension-test typechecks passed.\n- Targeted oxlint, oxfmt check, and `git diff --check` passed.\n- After ClawSweeper review, the focused public-policy test was simplified to use only the fields needed by the assertion; its focused test and the extension test-type lane passed again.\n- The aggregate `check:changed` wrapper could not reach its checks because its delegated Testbox dependency install hit the host's file-descriptor limit while fetching unrelated optional platform packages; the corresponding scoped typecheck/lint/test lanes above were run directly. Full hosted gates remain owned by PR CI.\n\nAll CLI and live verification used the OpenClaw repository source; it did not invoke Co-Claw.\n",
